Dear list,<br><br>I have two dataframes: trans and peakdata.<br><br><span> &gt; dput (trans)<br>structure(list(loc = c(1, 3, 18, 15, 22, 34, 50, 43, 90), fc = c(3.2, <br>4.5, 1.4, 1.1, 4.7, 5.1, 2, 5.2, 3.5)), .Names = c(&quot;loc&quot;, &quot;fc&quot;<br>
), row.names = c(NA, -9L), class = &quot;data.frame&quot;)<br>&gt; dput (peakdata)<br>structure(list(start = c(2, 10, 20, 45), end = c(4, 15, 21, 60<br>), testpeak = c(2, 5, 2, 7)), .Names = c(&quot;start&quot;, &quot;end&quot;, &quot;testpeak&quot;<br>
), row.names = c(NA, -4L), class = &quot;data.frame&quot;)<br><br><br>I would like to plot them, principally this way:<br><br>&gt; qm &lt;- ggplot (trans, aes(x=loc, y=fc))+ geom_point ()+geom_segment (data=peakdata, aes(x=start, xend=end, yend=0, y=testpeak), color=&quot;red&quot;)<br>
<br>Of course it would be much better to do it via faceting but I did not find a proper example for this using different dataframes. Could you please give me some instructions?<br>Thanks<br>Hermann<br></span>
